# R21 reveler conversations for the bell costume: logic from tools/content/build_fools_day_dialogue.py, lines drafted by Gemini (R21 revelers), edited.

~ doris_squire_start
doris_squire [smile]: Ring-a-ding, step in line, the law says every foot must rhyme! Shake your cuffs and clang the brass, no sour face is allowed to pass!
-> doris_squire_menu

~ doris_squire_menu
* [if flag.release_slips >= 1] Show them a release slip -> doris_squire_slip
* [Persuasion DC 15] Invite them to a better party, at a quiet church -> doris_squire_church | doris_squire_church_fail
* [Deception DC 15] Say Chuckles wants them at the church for the next number -> doris_squire_church | doris_squire_church_fail
* [knows:calm_emotions] Cast Calm Emotions on them -> doris_squire_calm
* [knows:greater_restoration] Cast Greater Restoration on them -> doris_squire_calm
* [if not flag.bell_tune_known and not flag.bell_tune_lost] Ask about the tune they keep humming -> doris_squire_tune
* [if flag.bell_tune_known] Hum the finished tune with them -> doris_squire_calm
* Knock them out of the costume, bruised but not hurt for good -> doris_squire_fight
* Leave them dancing for now -> END

~ doris_squire_slip
doris_squire [neutral]: Bloody hells, get this copper bucket off my shoulders. If anyone mentions a word of that prancing in my jailhouse, they will pay the fine twice over.
set release_slips -= 1
set reveler_doris_squire = "tickets"
set reveler_doris_squire_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ doris_squire_church
doris_squire [smile]: A grander peal down at the church, is there? Right then, march in step and keep the chimes ringing!
lead doris_squire to fd_silent_church
if check.last
set reveler_doris_squire = "church"
set reveler_doris_squire_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
set church_guests += 1
endif
-> END

~ doris_squire_church_fail
doris_squire [smile]: Naught doing, my beat is right here where the ribbons fly and the bells go clang! Move along or join the ring!
set fd_chuckles_amused
-> doris_squire_menu

~ doris_squire_calm
doris_squire [weary]: My tongue feels thick as boot leather and my ears are ringing foul. A constable ought to keep order, not caper about like a springtime hare.
set reveler_doris_squire = "uncharmed"
set reveler_doris_squire_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ doris_squire_fight
doris_squire [angry]: By order of the Lord of Fools, every frown is a breach of the peace! Dance when the bell rings, or I will clatter your bones to the cobblestones!
Narrator: The dancers nearby keep on dancing. Nobody here is going to remember a punch.
combat reveler_doris_squire

~ doris_squire_beaten
doris_squire [weary]: Fair clout, that, and I will not book you for assaulting the watch. Just unbuckle this damned bell before my neck gives out.
set reveler_doris_squire = "beaten"
set reveler_doris_squire_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ doris_squire_sheltered
doris_squire [weary]: No noise in here, thank the quiet rain and the sunflower's grace. Give me ten minutes on this bench and I will have my notebook straight again.
-> END

~ doris_squire_tune
doris_squire [smile]: Ding-dong, ding-dong, the rhyme comes round and then it drops right on the ground! Help me strike the closing chime, friends, before the measure loses time!
if not flag.free_bell_asked
quest free_the_bell asked
set free_bell_asked
endif
-> doris_squire_tune_menu

~ doris_squire_tune_menu
* [Performance DC 15] Finish the tune -> doris_squire_tune_ok | doris_squire_tune_fail
* [if item:jericho_banjo] Play the tune out on Jericho's banjo -> doris_squire_tune_banjo
* [Religion DC 13] Recall a Brightsinger hymn that ends it -> doris_squire_tune_ok | doris_squire_tune_fail
* [ends:free_the_bell] Give up on the tune -> doris_squire_tune_silenced
* Back to the others -> doris_squire_menu

~ doris_squire_tune_ok
doris_squire [smile]: There goes the note, clean and true, like rain upon the meadow rue. My head is clear, and this ridiculous brass harness has lost its grip on me.
quest free_the_bell done
set bell_tune_known
-> doris_squire_menu

~ doris_squire_tune_banjo
Narrator: A banjo is not a bell, but it knows how a song wants to end. The last bar lands and the little bells all ring together.
doris_squire [smile]: There goes the note, clean and true, like rain upon the meadow rue. My head is clear, and this ridiculous brass harness has lost its grip on me.
set bell_tune_banjo
quest free_the_bell done
set bell_tune_known
-> doris_squire_menu

~ doris_squire_tune_fail
doris_squire [smile]: No, no, that sours all the brass, and breaks the verse before it can pass! Back to the start of the chime we go!
-> doris_squire_tune_menu

~ doris_squire_tune_silenced
Narrator: The humming goes on without an ending, a little thinner each time round.
quest free_the_bell silenced
set bell_tune_lost
-> doris_squire_menu

~ weston_murdoch_start
weston_murdoch [smile]: Hark the brass and lift your heels, brothers and sisters, for the carnival chimes wash every heavy heart clean! Come swing in the ring and let your worries peal away!
-> weston_murdoch_menu

~ weston_murdoch_menu
* [if flag.release_slips >= 1] Show them a release slip -> weston_murdoch_slip
* [Persuasion DC 15] Invite them to a better party, at a quiet church -> weston_murdoch_church | weston_murdoch_church_fail
* [Deception DC 15] Say Chuckles wants them at the church for the next number -> weston_murdoch_church | weston_murdoch_church_fail
* [knows:calm_emotions] Cast Calm Emotions on them -> weston_murdoch_calm
* [knows:greater_restoration] Cast Greater Restoration on them -> weston_murdoch_calm
* [if not flag.bell_tune_known and not flag.bell_tune_lost] Ask about the tune they keep humming -> weston_murdoch_tune
* [if flag.bell_tune_known] Hum the finished tune with them -> weston_murdoch_calm
* Knock them out of the costume, bruised but not hurt for good -> weston_murdoch_fight
* Leave them dancing for now -> END

~ weston_murdoch_slip
weston_murdoch [neutral]: Merciful heavens, my throat is raw and my poor Joan must be frantic. That was no hymn of hope in my mouth, only a hollow jingle that would not let me breathe.
set release_slips -= 1
set reveler_weston_murdoch = "tickets"
set reveler_weston_murdoch_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ weston_murdoch_church
weston_murdoch [smile]: A chorus of gladness waiting at the church doors, you say? Lead on, friends, and I shall bring the loudest bell in the parish!
lead weston_murdoch to fd_silent_church
if check.last
set reveler_weston_murdoch = "church"
set reveler_weston_murdoch_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
set church_guests += 1
endif
-> END

~ weston_murdoch_church_fail
weston_murdoch [smile]: Leave the lanterns when the square is overflowing with song and sweetmeats? Never, friends, come clasp hands and spin until the steeple bows!
set fd_chuckles_amused
-> weston_murdoch_menu

~ weston_murdoch_calm
weston_murdoch [weary]: Praise the dawn that never comes, that clamor has finally let go of my ribs. A man could lose his whole soul inside a smile that wide.
set reveler_weston_murdoch = "uncharmed"
set reveler_weston_murdoch_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ weston_murdoch_fight
weston_murdoch [angry]: Do not silence the bells of joy, friends, or the chorus will have to chastise you! Every sinner must dance tonight, whether their knees be willing or broken!
Narrator: The dancers nearby keep on dancing. Nobody here is going to remember a punch.
combat reveler_weston_murdoch

~ weston_murdoch_beaten
weston_murdoch [weary]: A hard sermon to swallow, friends, though I thank you for sparing my teeth. Help me out of this bell-frame so I can find Joan and the little ones.
set reveler_weston_murdoch = "beaten"
set reveler_weston_murdoch_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ weston_murdoch_sheltered
weston_murdoch [weary]: To sit under a quiet vault again feels like cool water on a burn. My father died with a crowd jeering round the oak, and that square out there sounded dreadful close to it.
-> END

~ weston_murdoch_tune
weston_murdoch [smile]: Ring the high note, ring the low, yet where does the last little cadence go? Lend me your voice, friends, for the final bar keeps slipping from my tongue!
if not flag.free_bell_asked
quest free_the_bell asked
set free_bell_asked
endif
-> weston_murdoch_tune_menu

~ weston_murdoch_tune_menu
* [Performance DC 15] Finish the tune -> weston_murdoch_tune_ok | weston_murdoch_tune_fail
* [if item:jericho_banjo] Play the tune out on Jericho's banjo -> weston_murdoch_tune_banjo
* [Religion DC 13] Recall a Brightsinger hymn that ends it -> weston_murdoch_tune_ok | weston_murdoch_tune_fail
* [ends:free_the_bell] Give up on the tune -> weston_murdoch_tune_silenced
* Back to the others -> weston_murdoch_menu

~ weston_murdoch_tune_ok
weston_murdoch [smile]: Amen and amen, that last chord rang straight through the fog in my skull! Thank you, friends, I am my own man again.
quest free_the_bell done
set bell_tune_known
-> weston_murdoch_menu

~ weston_murdoch_tune_banjo
Narrator: A banjo is not a bell, but it knows how a song wants to end. The last bar lands and the little bells all ring together.
weston_murdoch [smile]: Amen and amen, that last chord rang straight through the fog in my skull! Thank you, friends, I am my own man again.
set bell_tune_banjo
quest free_the_bell done
set bell_tune_known
-> weston_murdoch_menu

~ weston_murdoch_tune_fail
weston_murdoch [smile]: Ah, that note rang flat and cold, so the merry carillon must be retold! Once more from the top, with brighter smiles!
-> weston_murdoch_tune_menu

~ weston_murdoch_tune_silenced
Narrator: The humming goes on without an ending, a little thinner each time round.
quest free_the_bell silenced
set bell_tune_lost
-> weston_murdoch_menu

